Package: cockpit-lxc
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         cockpit-bridge (>= 300),
         incus,
         incus-client
Recommends: cockpit-ws (>= 300)
Description: Cockpit user interface for LXC system containers
 Manage LXC system containers from the Cockpit web console: lifecycle,
 resource limits, network and disk devices, profiles, snapshots, images,
 and an interactive terminal.
 .
 The plugin reaches incusd over its local REST socket through
 cockpit-bridge, so it inherits Cockpit's authentication rather than
 introducing a second credential. It requires administrative access,
 because the Incus socket is owned by root:incus-admin.
 .
 incus-client is a hard dependency rather than a recommendation: Incus
 exposes exec and events as websockets, which cockpit.http cannot upgrade
 to, so the terminal and the live event stream are both carried by the
 incus binary.
